## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical multi-tenant streaming design, data contracts, lineage, schema evolution, late data, and engine trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Per-record contracts and schema registry
- Per-record lineage in metadata store
- Late data handling and watermarks
- Idempotent upserts into Iceberg
- Tenant isolation and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Contract check example (pseudo)
function validate(record, contract){
  for (const f of contract.fields){
    if (f.required && (record[f.name] === undefined || record[f.name] === null)) return false;
    // type checks omitted for brevity
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement a governance layer for schema evolution across tenants?
- What tests would you add to guard against drift in late-arriving records?

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates practical design skills for privacy-aware, scalable data ingestion, testing strategies, and architectural decision-making under regional compliance requirements.

## Key Concepts
- Centralized policy registry with dynamic privacy rule enforcement
- Per-record lineage tracking via unique identifiers
- Iceberg upserts with schema evolution support
- Regional isolation and late-data handling (up to 60 minutes)
- Privacy conformance tests and data-quality validation gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Policy application sketch
function applyPolicy(record, policyRegistry) {
  const policies = policyRegistry.getPolicies(record.region, record.dataType);
  return policies.reduce((r, policy) => policy.transform(r), record);
}
```
